# SCROLL while a reply is streaming: testdata/faux/qa/scroll-stream.yaml
# holds its response behind a 3s delay so the turn is still busy ("esc to
# interrupt") when the scroll lands. Checks the scroll itself doesn't
# corrupt anything and the streamed markers land intact once the turn
# finishes.
#
# What this does NOT establish (not traceable from source without a real
# run): whether the viewport auto-snaps back to the bottom once the turn
# settles while the user had scrolled up. internal/tui/app.go's transcript
# commit helper only calls viewport.GotoBottom() when wasBottom was true
# before the commit ("scroll-to-pause": follows the bottom only if it was
# already there) — which reads as "stays wherever the user left it," but
# that has not been confirmed against the running program here.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/scroll-stream.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE tell me about the rollout
KEY enter
WAITFOR /esc to stop/ 10
SHOT streaming-before-scroll

SCROLL up 3
SHOT streaming-during-scroll
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
WAIT 3.5
SHOT streaming-after-delay-still-scrolled
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/

# Scroll back down explicitly rather than assume auto-snap either way
# (see the header note): this is the reliable way to confirm the
# completed text landed intact once the turn is done.
SCROLL down 3
WAITFOR /STREAM-DONE-MARKER/ 20
SHOT streaming-done
EXPECT /STREAM-START-MARKER/
EXPECT /STREAM-DONE-MARKER/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
